                  X
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            In fact that horizontal morphism is an acyclic fibration in the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/folk+model+structure"} folk model structure
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-surjective+functor"} k-surjective functor
            for all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %p This is recalled in the following reference.
          %h4#principal_2bundles
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            \-principal 2-bundles
          %p
            For
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo =
                    %mn 2
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C = 2Cat
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B := \mathbf{B}G
            a strict one-object 2-groupoid corresponding to a strict
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-group"} 2-group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            with the unique point,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi E
                    %mi pt
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo =
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi E
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{E}_{pt} \mathbf{B}G = \mathbf{E}G
            was described under the name
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi INN
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} INN(G)
            in
          %ul
            %li
              Urs Schreiber, David Roberts,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The inner automorphism 3-group of a strict 2-group
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0708.1741v2"} arXiv
          %p
            This was shown to be
            %em action bigroupoid
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            acting on itself in
          %ul
            %li
              Igor Bakovič,
              %em Bigroupoid 2-torsors
              PhD thesis, Munich (2008) (
              %a{:href => "http://edoc.ub.uni-muenchen.de/9209/"}> pdf
              ).
          %p
            One can show that every
            = succeed "-principal" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Toby Bartels,
                %em 2-Bundles
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.CT/0410328"}> arXiv
                )
            %li
              %p
                Christoph Wockel,
                %em …
            %li
              %p
                Igor Bakovič,
                %em Bigroupoid 2-torsors
                PhD thesis, Munich (2008) (
                %a{:href => "http://edoc.ub.uni-muenchen.de/9209/"}> pdf
                ).
          %p
            indeed is recovered as the pullback of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi E
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{E} G \to \mathbf{B}G
            along the corresponding cocycle, along the lines described above.
          %p The way this works is indicated briefly in the last section of Roberts-Schreiber above. A more detailed description for the moment is in the notes
          %ul
            %li
              Urs Schreiber:
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/2bundrecon.pdf", :title => "G-principal 2-bundles from pullbacks of the 2-groupoidal EG"} G-principal 2-bundles from pullbacks of the 2-groupoidal EG
          %h3#UniversanNCategoryBundles
            Universal
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-subobject" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            One can take
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            to be something very different from the familiar classifying groupoids. Taking it to be
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n Cat
            yields the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject+classifiers"} subobject classifiers
            of higher
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} toposes
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi E
                        %mi pt
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi Cat
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi Cat
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{E}_{pt} (-1)Cat \to (-1)Cat
                is
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mo ⊤
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mo ⊤
                        %mo ,
                        %mo ⊥
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\top\} \to \{\top, \bottom\}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject+classifier"} subobject classifier
                in
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi E
                        %mi pt
                      %mn 0
                      %mi Cat
                      %mo →
                      %mn 0
                      %mi Cat
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{E}_{pt} 0Cat \to 0Cat
                is
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Set
                          %mo *
                        %mo →
                        %mi Set
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set_* \to Set
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+sets"} pointed sets
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject+classifier"} subobject classifier
                in
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+elements"} category of elements
                of a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi E
                        %mi pt
                      %mi Cat
                      %mo →
                      %mi Cat
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{E}_{pt} Cat \to Cat
                is
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Cat
                          %mo *
                        %mo →
                        %mi Cat
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat_* \to Cat
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction"} Grothendieck construction
          %p It was David Roberts in the blog comment
          %ul
            %li
              David Roberts,
              %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2008/01/101_things_to_do_with_a_2class.html#c014559"} comment in: 101 things to do with a 2-classifier
          %p who first pointed out that these (higher) subobject classifiers are just generalized universal bundles in the above sense.
          %p
            These cases for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n= 0
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n=1
            have been considered in the context of universal category bundles in
          %ul
            %li
              Kathryn Hess,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/HessLackBundCat.pdf", :title => "Bundle theory for categories"} Bundle theory for categories
              \.
          %p
            The discussion there becomes more manifestly one of bundles if one regards all morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \to Set
            appearing there as being the right legs of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anafunctors"} anafunctors
          %p
            There is a well-understood version of this for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = (\infty,1)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-categories
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+fibration+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} universal fibration of (∞,1)-categories
          %h3#action_groupoids_as_generalized_bundles Action groupoids as generalized bundles
          %p
            A morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo :
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho : B \to F
            to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+object"} pointed object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            (needs not be a basepoint preserving morphism!) can be regarded as a
            %em representation
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            on the point of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            = succeed "-bundle" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi E
                    %mi pt
                  %mi F
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho^* \mathbf{E}_{pt} F \to B
          %p
            can be addressed as the
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              \-bundle
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ρ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
                \-associated
              to the universal
              = succeed "-bundle" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi E
                        %mi pt
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{E}_{pt}B
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            is a groupoid, then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi E
                    %mi pt
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho^* \mathbf{E}_{pt} F
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+groupoid"} action groupoid
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            acting on the point of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
          %p
            Further pulling this back along a cocycle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g : \hat X \to B
            of a
            = succeed "-principal" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            = succeed "-accociated" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
          %p
            For instance for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo =
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B = \mathbf{B}G
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo =
                  %mi Vect
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F = Vect
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi Vect
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho : \mathbf{B}G \to Vect
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation"} representation
            of the group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            on a vector space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed "-associated" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
            = succeed "-bundle" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Vect
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Vect}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo →
                  %mi V
                  %mo ⫽
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  V \to V \sslash G \to \mathbf{B}G
                  \\,.
          %p
            Pulling that further back along the cocycle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g : \hat X \to \mathbf{B}G
            classifying a
            = succeed "-principal" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mi G
                  %mi V
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \times_G V \to X
            which is
            = succeed "-associated" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi g
                            %mo *
                          %msup
                            %mi ρ
                            %mo *
                          %msub
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi E
                            %mi pt
                          %mi F
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mo ≃
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi P
                          %msub
                            %mo ×
                            %mi G
                          %mi V
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↙
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  g^* \rho^*\mathbf{E}_{pt}F
                  \&amp;&amp;\stackrel{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}&amp;&amp; P\times_G V
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp;
                  X
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            For more on this see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-action"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                  \-action
          %h2#related_pages Related pages
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration+sequence"} fibration sequence
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limit"} homotopy limit
